Items I find on the floor, in chests, and as death-drops,
are typically a main source of objects, and specifically
of _that object that I was talking about_; the scroll of
enchant weapon. While you, OTOH, seem to be focussing on
monster equipment, which contributes to a huge degree to
only a _specific subset_ of all objects. - I think those
are two different topics. - Scrolls of enchant weapon are
(AFAIK) never part of the monster equipment. But they are
generated as [random] death-drops, as [random] objects in
shops (in general shops, or in scroll shops, etc.), or as
[random] contents of containers. All those occurrences
seem to be subject to that random generation probability
where scrolls are involved. Typically this scroll (in my
games) occurs quite frequently. And interestingly, once
I reach Moloch's Sanctum's morgue (where I often already
had enchanted my weapon(s) to their maximum) I typically
find a lot more scrolls of enchant weapons in the chests
of that morgue level, as if the RNG tries to support me
vaporising my enchanted artifact weapon in an accident.

(The Wiki says: "Scrolls constitute 16% of all randomly-
generated items in the main dungeon, 18% in containers".
And the scroll of enchant weapon has this 8% probability
of those random scrolls generated. This is quite a lot!)

